# `--allocator debug` (plans/backlog/ZIG_ADOPTION_CANDIDATES.md Z11):
# tests/debug_allocator.test.yo checks the debug allocator's aborts (double
# free, foreign pointer, write after free) and its exit verdict only when the
# program runs on it. The language suite runs that file under the default
# allocator; this case is its `debug` run, where every test runs and every
# parent test must itself end with no live block. Only the summary is kept:
# the batch compile's chatter moves with the compiler.
stdout_keep=^(\$ yo |rc=|.*[0-9]+ passed|.*[0-9]+ failed|yo: error)
timeout=900
